# Liquid Dreaming

The first project made with this machine, and the reason it was built.

<!-- photo d'ouverture : une impression en suspension dans le bain, prise à travers le gel -->

## The project

Liquid Dreaming is a methodological platform. Dream narratives are passed through the latent
space of a model, semantic trajectories are extracted from it, and those trajectories become
the geometry printed inside the gel. The dreams are not the point, they are the entry that
made sense.

This folder documents the printing side of the project: how the shapes get made physically.

## Why print inside a gel

Soft matter laid in open air can only build what gravity allows. It slumps, it spreads, it
falls. Printing into a support bath removes that limit.

The bath used here is a Carbopol gel. It is transparent and self-healing: it opens ahead of
the needle and closes behind it. What is deposited stays where it was deposited, held in
suspension for the length of the print. Shapes that could not stand on their own become
printable.

